   "source": [
    "# 🔬 ForensicFusion - Kaggle Training Notebook\n",
    "**Multi-Expert Deep Learning for AI-Generated & Manipulated Image Detection**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "### ⚡ Prerequisites\n",
    "1. In the right sidebar, under **Notebook options**, set **Accelerator** to **GPU T4 x2** (or P100).\n",
    "2. Under **Internet**, toggle to **On**.\n",
    "3. Add the dataset: click **+ Add data** → search for `awsaf49/artifact-dataset` (or your dataset name) → **Add**.\n",
    "4. If resuming from a previous checkpoint, upload your `latest.pt` as a **Kaggle Dataset** (see Step 3)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Verify GPU Availability\n",
    "!nvidia-smi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📦 Step 1: Clone Repository & Install Dependencies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clone the ForensicFusion GitHub repository\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/shaheerzafarr/ForensicFusion.git\n",
    "%cd ForensicFusion\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install dependencies\n",
    "!pip install -q pyyaml pandas numpy pillow tqdm scikit-learn transformers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📂 Step 2: Setup Working Directories & Copy Data Files"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create working directories\n",
    "os.makedirs('/kaggle/working/checkpoints', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs('/kaggle/working/logs', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs('/kaggle/working/data', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Copy data files from repo to working dir\n",
    "!cp -v data/generators.json /kaggle/working/data/\n",
    "!cp -v data/splits.csv /kaggle/working/data/ 2>/dev/null || echo 'No splits.csv yet (will be created)'\n",
    "!cp -v data/artifact_index.csv /kaggle/working/data/ 2>/dev/null || echo 'No artifact_index.csv yet (will be created)'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify dataset is mounted\n",
    "print('\\n📂 Available input datasets:')\n",
    "!ls /kaggle/input/\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find the actual dataset path\n",
    "import glob\n",
    "candidates = glob.glob('/kaggle/input/*/') + glob.glob('/kaggle/input/*/*/')\n",
    "for c in candidates:\n",
    "    print(f'  {c}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🔄 Step 3: Resume from Checkpoint (Optional)\n",
    "\n",
    "**To resume training from a previous session:**\n",
    "1. Go to [kaggle.com/datasets/new](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/new)\n",
    "2. Upload your `latest.pt` file as a new dataset (name it e.g. `forensicfusion-checkpoint`)\n",
    "3. In this notebook, click **+ Add data** in the right sidebar → search for your checkpoint dataset → **Add**\n",
    "4. Update the path in the cell below to match your dataset name"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import shutil\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# OPTION A: Resume from uploaded checkpoint dataset\n",
    "# Change this path to match your uploaded checkpoint dataset name\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "CHECKPOINT_DATASET = '/kaggle/input/forensicfusion-checkpoint'  # <-- change this\n",
    "\n",
    "checkpoint_found = False\n",
    "\n",
    "# Search for latest.pt in all input datasets\n",
    "search_paths = [\n",
    "    f'{CHECKPOINT_DATASET}/latest.pt',\n",
    "    f'{CHECKPOINT_DATASET}/checkpoints/latest.pt',\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Also search all input directories\n",
    "for root, dirs, files in os.walk('/kaggle/input/'):\n",
    "    for f in files:\n",
    "        if f == 'latest.pt':\n",
    "            search_paths.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n",
    "\n",
    "for path in search_paths:\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(path):\n",
    "        shutil.copy2(path, '/kaggle/working/checkpoints/latest.pt')\n",
    "        size_mb = os.path.getsize('/kaggle/working/checkpoints/latest.pt') / (1024*1024)\n",
    "        print(f'✅ Checkpoint restored from: {path} ({size_mb:.1f} MB)')\n",
    "        checkpoint_found = True\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "if not checkpoint_found:\n",
    "    print('ℹ️  No checkpoint found — training will start fresh from Epoch 1')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Peek at checkpoint metadata\n",
    "    import torch\n",
    "    ckpt = torch.load('/kaggle/working/checkpoints/latest.pt', map_location='cpu')\n",
    "    print(f'   Epoch: {ckpt.get(\"epoch\", \"?\")}, Step: {ckpt.get(\"step\", \"?\")}, Global Step: {ckpt.get(\"global_step\", \"?\")}')\n",
    "    print(f'   Best AUC: {ckpt.get(\"best_auc\", \"?\")}')\n",
    "    del ckpt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🎯 Step 4: Start Training\n",
    "Uses `config_kaggle.yaml` which is optimized for Kaggle T4 GPUs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Start Training with Kaggle-optimized config\n",
    "!python train.py --config config_kaggle.yaml"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 💾 Step 5: Download Checkpoints Before Shutting Down\n",
    "**⚠️ IMPORTANT: Run this cell BEFORE ending your Kaggle session!**\n",
    "\n",
    "Kaggle's `/kaggle/working/` is ephemeral — files are lost when the session ends.\n",
    "This cell lets you download `latest.pt` and `best.pt` to your local machine."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 60)\n",
    "print('📦 CHECKPOINT STATUS')\n",
    "print('=' * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "checkpoint_dir = '/kaggle/working/checkpoints'\n",
    "files_to_download = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for fname in os.listdir(checkpoint_dir):\n",
    "    fpath = os.path.join(checkpoint_dir, fname)\n",
    "    if fname.endswith('.pt') and not fname.endswith('.tmp'):\n",
    "        size_mb = os.path.getsize(fpath) / (1024*1024)\n",
    "        files_to_download.append((fname, fpath, size_mb))\n",
    "        print(f'  ✅ {fname} ({size_mb:.1f} MB)')\n",
    "\n",
    "if not files_to_download:\n",
    "    print('  ❌ No checkpoint files found!')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Peek at latest.pt metadata\n",
    "    latest_path = os.path.join(checkpoint_dir, 'latest.pt')\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(latest_path):\n",
    "        import torch\n",
    "        ckpt = torch.load(latest_path, map_location='cpu')\n",
    "        print(f'\\n  📊 latest.pt → Epoch {ckpt.get(\"epoch\", \"?\")}, '\n",
    "              f'Step {ckpt.get(\"step\", \"?\")}, '\n",
    "              f'Global Step {ckpt.get(\"global_step\", \"?\")}, '\n",
    "              f'Best AUC {ckpt.get(\"best_auc\", \"?\")}')\n",
    "        del ckpt\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\n' + '=' * 60)\n",
    "print('⬇️  DOWNLOAD OPTIONS')\n",
    "print('=' * 60)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Option 1: Click the files in the right sidebar under \"Output\"')\n",
    "print('          (/kaggle/working/checkpoints/)')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Option 2: Use the Kaggle API from your local machine:')\n",
    "print('          kaggle kernels output <your-username>/<notebook-slug>')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Option 3: Programmatic download (uncomment the cell below)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# === OPTION 3: Copy checkpoints to /kaggle/working/ root for easy download ===\n",
    "# Files in /kaggle/working/ appear in the \"Output\" tab of your notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "checkpoint_dir = '/kaggle/working/checkpoints'\n",
    "\n",
    "for fname in ['latest.pt', 'best.pt']:\n",
    "    src = os.path.join(checkpoint_dir, fname)\n",
    "    dst = f'/kaggle/working/{fname}'\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(src):\n",
    "        shutil.copy2(src, dst)\n",
    "        size_mb = os.path.getsize(dst) / (1024 * 1024)\n",
    "        print(f'✅ Copied {fname} to /kaggle/working/ ({size_mb:.1f} MB)')\n",
    "        print(f'   → Download from Output tab or via: kaggle kernels output <user>/<notebook>')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f'⚠️  {fname} not found in {checkpoint_dir}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Also copy training logs\n",
    "log_src = '/kaggle/working/logs/training.csv'\n",
    "if os.path.exists(log_src):\n",
    "    shutil.copy2(log_src, '/kaggle/working/training_log.csv')\n",
    "    print(f'✅ Copied training log to /kaggle/working/training_log.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\n🎉 All files are now in /kaggle/working/ — check the Output tab!')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
